# Design principles

Full reference: `docs/design-principles.md` (from [emilkowalski/skills](https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills)).

## Hard rules

- Color and type live in `app/globals.css` semantic aliases (proposal paper / ink / deep blue / sky). `@loople/tokens` is motion-only — do not fork a second palette, toast, or button system.
- Animate only when frequency + purpose pass the gate; never animate keyboard / 100+/day actions.
- Prefer CSS transitions; animate `transform`/`opacity` only; never `scale(0)` or `ease-in` on UI; keep UI motion ≤300ms.
- Gate hover with `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- One Sonner `<Toaster />` in root layout; use Radix/shadcn for dialogs/menus — do not hand-roll.
- Mobile: no `maximum-scale=1` as a zoom fix; inputs ≥16px on touch; prefer `dvh`/`svh` over `100vh`.
- When reviewing UI/motion, report findings as a `| Before | After | Why |` table.
